From 06c2981723919f2ed157559c946fb8b4187e502d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Blake Williams <blake.williams@parrylabs.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:02:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] tee: optee: ffa: fix build failing to compile without
 Tegra264 support

get_reserved_shm_region() returns -ENOTSUP when ARCH_TEGRA_264_SOC or TEGRA_HV_DRIVER is disabled.
ENOTSUP is not defined in the kernel, so OP-TEE driver fails to compile:

	drivers/tee/optee/ffa_abi.c: In function 'get_reserved_shm_region':
	drivers/tee/optee/ffa_abi.c:571:17: error: 'ENOTSUP' undeclared

Return -EOPNOTSUPP instead. Caller checks for any non-zero value, so behavior should be unchanged.

Fixes: f5c7dedfac27 ("NVIDIA: SAUCE: tee: optee: ffa: add static shared memory support")
Upstream-Status: Submitted https://forums.developer.nvidia.com/t/r39-2-1-kernel-op-tee-fails-to-compile-when-arch-tegra-264-soc-is-disabled-enotsup-undeclared/389524
Signed-off-by: Blake Williams <blake.williams@parrylabs.com>
---
 drivers/tee/optee/ffa_abi.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/tee/optee/ffa_abi.c b/drivers/tee/optee/ffa_abi.c
index 3d35130bd..b006f6086 100644
--- a/drivers/tee/optee/ffa_abi.c
+++ b/drivers/tee/optee/ffa_abi.c
@@ -568,7 +568,7 @@ static int get_reserved_shm_region(phys_addr_t *paddr, size_t *size)
 
 	return ret;
 #else
-	return -ENOTSUP;
+	return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 #endif
 }
 
